ure which I would like to  call your pre trained ception  okay so let's dive into it from now on  we will call this the transformer module  which is formed like we have explained  in the last video so it is formed of the  multi-head self attention layer the  feed-forward layers in the residual  connections acting like information  highways between them so this everything  now is the transformer module the trick  here is to train the model on text image  pairs like images and their captions the  text part is easy to explain because it  is exactly like what the usual pert  architecture does we feeds the word or  tokens in vector representation together  after we added the positional embeddings  or identifiers to these vectors so our  model is informed about the word order  by these positional embeddings and we  feed this to our usual transformer  module to process the text now let's put  the text part to the side a little bit  and see what we can do on the image side  we also have to somehow transform our  image into a vector sequence format  because the transformer is specialized  for exactly this sequences but but how  well the idea is if we combine vision  and language anyway why not have an  architecture that specializes on finding  correspondences between words and image  regions regions there we said it let's  extract such image regions and order  them in an arbitrary sequence we can  represent each region by a vector  by employing CNN based neural network  that we borrow from computer vision good  we got this far now the idea is to  really compute these correspondences  between image regions and the text by  adding the layers that to this  computation with Co attention now what  does Co attention mean until now we had  attention we had self attention now we  have Co attention well while the usual  transformer modules in green look only  at their own branch for computing  attention through self attention the  cool attention modules in blue are  looking also at the other branch to  compute important scores between images  and text and vice versa  so with Co attention the image computes  attention based on the text and vice  versa for refinement we add then another  layer of Transformers and another Co  attention layer and another transformer  module and another and you get it the  deeper the better we are doing deep  learning here huh  now the question is how do we end this  how do we get to our output and what is  our output anyway well it depends what  we train our network to do it can be  just a multi-layer perceptron followed  by a soft max for getting out of score  for example for the similarity between  image and text this is really dependent  on the task and the whole network can  have many of these output heads one for  each task it is trained on and sometimes  it is trained also in parallel on many  different tasks so naturally we have to  discuss what with train this monster to  do in this pre train inception how I  like to call it it is a very interesting  part because like in every inception we  have multiple stages and here we are  ready to explain what stage one is we do  pre training at this first stage on the  text side end on the image side but  separately for the text we have birds  trained on huge amounts of English text  so we take that birth weights and use  them here to initialize our word modules  then the image side has to be also pre  trained to produce useful features from  the images here in the Wilbert paper  they have used our faster our CNN  architecture useful in object detection  for computer vision for the second stage  of pre-training the wilpert paper uses  their conceptual captions data set they  use this one and no other because it is  huge and contains images and their  captions and on this conceptual captions  data set they train the network that was  already trained on english text  welder with the following objectives one  task is to predict labels for what the  image regions might be another training  task is also followed at this stage  which is masked word prediction like in  the classical transformer so here the  model would ideally predict mountain  because it knows from the image through  Co attention layers  what should fall into that place best  and we are already at a training stage  number three where the same model that  at stage one learned to process images  and text separately at stage two  combines them and understands the  relations between text and image and is  now ready to be trained to solve a task  involving both textual and visual  modalities such tasks are for example  visual question and answering where the  model is given an image and the question  and it has to provide the right answer  to the question based on the image  Wilbert not only beat the state of the  art at the time of publication on this  task but by a large margin visual  common-sense reasoning is the better  brother of visual question and answering  where the system has to provide the  answer to the question but also to give  the reason for the answer and ideally  this reason is you know reasoning about  a problem and is not giving tautological  ination like this picture is a mountain  because it is a mountain but rather an  explanation that this image depicts a  mountain because if the mountain is  taller than the horizon for example here  Wilbert also achieved state of the art  by a large margin image retrieval is the  task where given a caption of an image  the model has to select the right image  it is described by the caption from a  pool of many other images and surprise  surprise state of the art again  kohrville Burt phrase grounding is a  more fine-grained task but also perfect  for Wilbert that thanks to the Coe  attention layers learns relationships  between image regions and words because  here in this task given a phrase in the  caption like mountain the system has to  identify the region that this phrase  refers to and yes again state of the art  for Wilbert so now that you have seen  training in so many stages first on text  on images then on text and images and  you have seen how this has helped  Wilbert to perform so well on many  downstream tasks we can sell free say  that is whole pre-trained ception  or you know different stages or  strategies to pre train the model before  being applied and trained further on a  downstream task is really really helpful  and because these pre training  strategies are so cool we will spend the  whole next video only about this we will  discuss different pre training  strategies because Wilbert follows only  two of the pre training strategies but  there are others propose in other papers  about multimodal transformers so we will  see these strategies in the next video  and not only strategies for multimodal  transformers but also for the pure  language bird see you then  [Music]  you  [Music]

